== The Deal

J floor exists to give builders in Zurich a space to build. We are a community of
founders, tech builders, and researchers at the earliest stages of their journey.
We believe in showing up, getting our hands dirty, and supporting one another
along the way.

*What we offer.* Free workspace and a curated community of founders building in
it. Someone makes their first sale, someone gets stuck on a problem you solved
last week, someone needs an intro you can make. We optimize for high-agency,
boldness, hard work, and organic connections.

There are no membership fees. No equity taken, no structured deals. The space is
funded by sponsors who believe in what we are building. See Sponsor Transparency
below.

You can access J floor spaces via a combination of digital and physical access,
24/7.

*For who.* People working on early stage projects looking for a community to
build with.

*What we expect.* You need access to the space because you are actively working
on something. You show up, and you participate. Help others, share what you know,
give tips, make warm intros. Give before you get.

== Admission

To join J floor, you need first a recommendation from a community member. The
Board reviews applications and admits new members monthly. Until your membership
is confirmed, you may be invited as a guest. The guest period is handled case by
case. By coming as a guest to J floor, you agree to the terms below.

== Main Rules

*Show up.* J floor works because people are here.

*Build.* We do not gatekeep on entry, but we expect you to be working on
something real.

*Participate.* Help others. Share what you know. Make introductions. The best
communities are built by people who give more than they take.

*Respect.* Treat the space and the people in it with care. Be someone others want
to work alongside. We have zero tolerance for disrespectful behavior or
discrimination.

*Confidentiality.* Respect the privacy of other members. What you see on someone's
screen, overhear in conversation, or learn about their work stays within the
community. Treat it as confidential.

*Association confidentiality.* By coming as a guest to J floor, you agree to
maintain the confidentiality of all non-public information relating to the
Association, including but not limited to financial data, sponsor arrangements,
strategic plans, and Board decisions. This obligation survives termination of
guest access.

For day-to-day space rules, see the J floor Space Guide.

== Sponsor Transparency

J floor is funded by sponsors who support the founder ecosystem. We are
founder-first. Sponsors do not receive equity in your company, structured deals,
or early rights of any kind. We share limited, non-sensitive information about
members and guests with sponsors to provide visibility into the community. For
full details on what is shared and how your data is handled, see our Privacy
Policy.

== Termination

The Board may terminate your guest access at any time in cases where the space,
other users, or the spirit of the community is not respected. This includes, but
is not limited to, inactivity or failure to build. Termination requires a majority
Board decision, with written notification. Upon termination, access to the space
will be revoked.

== Intellectual Property

What you build is yours. J floor makes no claim to any intellectual property,
ideas, code, products, or ventures created by members.

== Liability

You use J floor at your own risk. J floor is not responsible for loss, theft, or
damage to personal belongings or equipment. We recommend you have your own
insurance. J floor is not liable for injuries, losses, or damages arising from
your use of the space.

== Data Protection

J floor collects and processes personal data in accordance with applicable Swiss
data protection law. We only process what is necessary for membership
administration and the purposes described in this agreement. You have the right to
access, correct, or request deletion of your data at any time. For full details,
see our Privacy Policy.

== Amendments

J floor may update this agreement. Members and guests will be notified of material
changes with reasonable notice. Continued use of the space after changes take
effect constitutes acceptance.

== Legal Bits

J floor is a Swiss association (Verein) under Art. 60 ff. of the Swiss Civil Code.
This agreement is governed by Swiss law. The courts of Zurich have exclusive
jurisdiction.
